<!-- Cloud Backup -->
<section class="bg-slate-50 dark:bg-navy-900 py-16 lg:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center">
      <!-- Illustrative panel (no photo asset needed) -->
      <div class="order-last lg:order-2">
        <div class="relative rounded-xl shadow-xl bg-linear-to-br from-navy-800 via-navy-900 to-navy-950 p-8 lg:p-10 overflow-hidden">
          <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-topo-pattern opacity-30 pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="relative z-10 flex flex-col items-center text-center">
            <div class="w-20 h-20 rounded-2xl bg-sky-500/15 flex items-center justify-center mb-6">
              <!-- Cloud + upload icon -->
              <svg class="w-10 h-10 text-sky-400" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M17.5 19a4.5 4.5 0 0 0 .5-8.96A6 6 0 0 0 6.34 9.1 4.5 4.5 0 0 0 7 18h2"/>
                <path d="M12 12v7"/>
                <path d="m9 15 3-3 3 3"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <p class="font-mono text-xs tracking-wider text-sky-300/80 mb-2">SQUAWK 1200 &bull; YOUR STORAGE</p>
            <p class="text-white font-semibold text-lg">Your backup. Your destination. Your keys.</p>
            <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-2 text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-300">
              <span class="px-2 py-1 rounded bg-white/5 border border-white/10">S3-compatible</span>
              <span class="px-2 py-1 rounded bg-white/5 border border-white/10">WebDAV</span>
              <span class="px-2 py-1 rounded bg-white/5 border border-white/10">Nextcloud</span>
              <span class="px-2 py-1 rounded bg-white/5 border border-white/10">Your own server</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal lg:order-1">
        <span class="freq-badge mb-4">
          <span class="inline-block w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-400 animate-blink"></span>
          NEW &bull; USER-OWNED
        </span>
        <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-800 dark:text-white mb-4 mt-3">Cloud Backup</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Send a copy of your logbook to a cloud storage location <em>you</em> own and control &mdash; on a schedule, automatically. Point NinerLog at your S3 bucket, your Nextcloud, your home NAS, or any provider you trust, and we&rsquo;ll keep an offsite copy of your flights there for you. No NinerLog-only vault, no lock-in &mdash; just your data, in your storage.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-3">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-500 mt-0.5 shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
            <span class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300"><strong>You pick the destination.</strong> Bring your own bucket or server &mdash; NinerLog never holds the only copy</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-500 mt-0.5 shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
            <span class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300"><strong>Truly user-owned.</strong> The backup files sit in your storage account under your credentials &mdash; you can read, copy, or delete them without us</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-500 mt-0.5 shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
            <span class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300"><strong>Open formats.</strong> Backups use the same CSV / JSON your export already produces &mdash; readable with or without NinerLog</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-500 mt-0.5 shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
            <span class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300"><strong>Opt-in and reversible.</strong> Off by default, switch on when you want it, disconnect any time &mdash; we keep no copy of your storage credentials beyond what&rsquo;s needed to run the backup</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-500 mt-0.5 shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
            <span class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300"><strong>Scheduled, offsite, automatic.</strong> A second copy lands safely outside the app on the cadence you choose &mdash; daily, weekly, or after every flight</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-500 mt-0.5 shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
            <span class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300"><strong>Restore from your own files.</strong> Bring a backup file back into NinerLog at any time &mdash; or open it directly in a spreadsheet</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
          Cloud backup is entirely optional &mdash; the rest of NinerLog works exactly the same with it switched off. See our <a href="/privacy" class="text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400 hover:underline">privacy policy</a> for how connection details are handled.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

